==Notes==
*[[Ranger]]s are prohibited from selecting this feat (on a ranger level), presumably because they receive the [[dual-wield (feat)|dual-wield]] feat at first level. (The ''dual-wield'' feat combines the effects of ''ambidexterity'' and [[two-weapon fighting]], as long as the ranger is not wearing [[medium armor|medium]] or [[heavy armor]], but does not qualify as a prerequisite for ''improved two-weapon fighting''.)

